abstract: >-
  Exact minimum sizes of Kochen-Specker sets inside nine finite coordinate ray pools
  (31 and 33 rays in dimension 3, 18 in dimension 4, 29 in dimension 5). Zero-Mathlib Lean 4.35.0
  kernel proofs cover B(3,2) = 31 and B(4,1) = 18 only; they are accepted by the official Lean
  kernel (default and paranoid mode) and by lean4lean, nanoda, con-leche and con-ron. The other
  seven values rest on SAT/DRUP unsatisfiability proofs checked by the project's own checker
  (cross-checked by drat-trim/LRAT for B(3,3)), a CNF encoder and paper lemmas. The general
  minimum problem is not affected. The values 31 (B(3,2), B(3,3)) and 33 (sixth roots of unity)
  were reported earlier by Kernaghan (arXiv:2603.16988), whose version 10 (23 November 2026) also
  proves 31 and 33 for two pools in Lean. Research preprint; not externally peer reviewed;
  AI-assisted under human direction.
